      "text": "⚡️🇵🇰 The Pakistan Army has instructed its warfighters and administrative personnel to phase out Meta-owned WhatsApp for official communications and transition to China’s WeChat platform.\n\nIslamabad initiated the shift due to growing cybersecurity concerns over Western platforms, citing heightened risks of surveillance, data breaches, and interception of sensitive conversations, according to local Pakistani media.\n\nSources trace the directive to an internal order, though Pakistan’s Inter-Services Public Relations wing has not issued a formal public statement confirming the change.\n\nCurrently, the Tencent-developed application and its domestic Chinese counterpart Weixin serve approximately 1.43 billion active users per month.\n\n@medmannews",
